        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Harrods Creek, Louisville, Jefferson County, Kentucky, Fayette\n- Topics: Louisville–Jefferson County merger, population ranking\n\nFacts:\n- Jefferson County is a county in the U.S. state of Kentucky.\n- Jefferson County is the most populous county in Kentucky and has more than twice the population of Fayette, the second most populous county.\n- In 2003, Harrods Creek was designated a neighborhood of Louisville when Louisville merged with Jefferson County.\n- Before 2003, Harrods Creek was an unincorporated community.",
